# AI tutor chat backend conventions

## Prompt assembly contract (POST /api/chat)

The system prompt is assembled in tiers, in this order:

1. `core` = `GLOBAL_BASE_RULES` + `persona.prompt` + `AGENT_PROMPTS[agentId]`
   (always present). Placeholders `{{userName}}`, `{{agentName}}`,
   `{{DREAM_SUBJECT}}`, `{{INSIGHT_PACKAGE}}` are substituted here.
2. `recent_activity` = the small `RECENT_ACTIVITY_GUIDANCE` block
   (only when the student has recent quests OR a recent mock).
3. `rag` = capped at `MAX_RAG_CHARS = 600`. Skip the placeholder
   "No specific snippets found." string from `KnowledgeService`.
4. `strategy` = `ACE_SIR_INJECTION` (only when `routeRequest` flags
   strategy keywords).
5. `lang_skip` = NATIVE HK SPEAKER MODE topics, capped to
   `MAX_LANG_SKIP_TOPICS = 8` then `+N more`.
6. `windowed` = a `[CONTEXT_SUMMARY] N earlier turn(s) omitted` line
   added only when `buildHistoryWindow` dropped messages.

Always log `tierFlags.join('+')` as `prompt_tier` via
`TokenService.logUsage(uid, 'chat', usageMetadata, { prompt_tier, agent_id, history_msgs, router_skipped, persona_id })`.
`persona_id` is the resolved tutor card id from `UserProfileService.getPersona` (null for guests / missing id).

## History window contract

- `MAX_TURNS = 12` and `MAX_CHARS_PER_MSG = 800` enforced in
  `buildHistoryWindow`. Frontend mirrors a `MAX_PAYLOAD_TURNS = 24`
  slice for wire size only - server is authoritative.
- Final content array MUST start with role `user` (Gemini constraint).
- Image data is attached to the LAST user turn; do not reorder turns.

## Intent router fast-path

Bypass `IntentRouter.classify` only when ALL of the following hold:

- `agentId !== 'math'`
- no image attached
- `CacheService.isGreetingOrAck(message)` returns true
- `CacheService.hasRecentLabProposal(history)` returns false

When in doubt, let the router run. Confirmation phrases like
"yes", "ok", "proceed", "好呀" intentionally are NOT in
`isGreetingOrAck` because they may be lab confirmations.

## Insight pack

`UserProfileService.formatInsightsForPrompt(pContext)` emits TWO lines:

- `[STUDENT_INSIGHTS]` - long-lived skill / quest snapshot
- `[RECENT_ACTIVITY] QUESTS:... | MOCK:...`

`pContext.recentMock` is sourced from
`users/{uid}/progress/mock_summary` (written by
`UserProfileService.saveMockSummary`). `pContext.recentQuests`
comes from `GamificationService.getRecentQuestSummary` which reads
`users/{uid}/quest_results`.

When you add a new mock submit endpoint, you MUST call
`UserProfileService.saveMockSummary(uid, { paper, topic, score,
total, percentage, level, topMistakes })` after the assessment.

## Don't

- Don't edit `backend/.env` or `backend/system_prompts.js` casually -
  they are governed elsewhere and may be `.cursorignore`d.
- Don't reintroduce unbounded `clientHistory` mapping. Always go
  through `buildHistoryWindow`.
- Don't add long static text to the system prompt without a
  corresponding `tierFlags.push(...)` so telemetry attributes it.
